and we sum over all $n_{\rm fit}-w+1$ full windows. Here $n_{\rm fit}=400$ is the number of scored levels; we avoid the letter $N$, which in this chapter is a grid size. Each $x_j^2$ appears in at most $w$ windows, each time with weight $1/w$, so $\sum_n B_w(x)_n^2\le\sum_jx_j^2$. To form mean squares, divide the left side by the number of full windows and the right side by $n_{\rm fit}$:
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{rms}(x)\;\ge\;\sqrt{\frac{n_{\rm fit}-w+1}{n_{\rm fit}}}\;\mathrm{rms}\big(B_w(x)\big).\label{eq:paper-spurious-floor-edge}
\end{equation}
Apply this to $x=d-m$, using $B_w(d-m)=B_w(d)$. The rms of the residual is at least the rms of $B_w(d)$ times the edge factor $\sqrt{(n_{\rm fit}-w+1)/n_{\rm fit}}$, which exceeds $0.98$ for $w\le13$ and $n_{\rm fit}=400$.
